      "file_name": "scaler-notes.md",
      "file_size": 492,
      "file_type": "text/markdown",
      "extracted_content": "SCALER NOTES\n\nThe tool takes a recipe written for one batch size and rewrites every quantity for another.\nThree things it has to get right:\n1. Units that do not scale linearly. Baking time is the obvious one. Salt is the awkward one.\n2. Fractions people actually use. 1/3 of 3/4 cup should read as a spoon measure, not 0.25 cup.\n3. Eggs. Half an egg is not a thing anyone wants in a printed recipe, so round and say so.\n\nKnown gap: no idea yet what to do about a recipe that names a tin size."
     }
