      "start_timestamp": "2026-05-04T09:33:49.000000Z",
      "stop_timestamp": "2026-05-04T09:33:52.800000Z",
      "flags": null,
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Paste this under Scaling rules:\n\n```\nscale(recipe, from, to):\n  ratio = to / from\n  for each ingredient:\n    if ingredient.counts_whole:      # eggs, tins, sheets\n      round to nearest whole, and note what was rounded\n    else:\n      pick the measure a cook owns, then the nearest amount it can hold\n  never scale: baking time, tin size, oven temperature\n  if the recipe names a tin, refuse and print the area ratio instead\n```\n\nThe last line is the one that matters: refusing is a result, not a failure.",
      "citations": []
     }
    ],
